# Talon's Junction: from the emulator's Time Trial start line, over speed pad 0.
#
# Planned, not hand-tuned. Regenerate with:
#
#   cargo run -q -p oag-trace -- plan --source data/images/pulse-psp-usa.chd \
#       --pad 0 --start 6.07,-50.07,-196.10 \
#       --look-min 26 --look-speed 0.55 --deadband 0.045 \
#       --out verification/scenarios/talons-junction-pad-0.inputs
#
# In our simulation this crosses the pad plane on tick 161 at (168.2, -48.0,
# -179.0) - 0.09 units right of the pad's centre line, inside a half width of
# 4.8 - doing 110.8, and is inside the pad's own trigger box from tick 159.
# Check it with:
#
#   cargo run -q -p oag-trace -- drive verification/scenarios/talons-junction-pad-0.inputs \
#       --source data/images/pulse-psp-usa.chd --start 6.07,-50.07,-196.10 --every 20
#
# The first two ticks are deliberately empty: `psp-trace.py --script-lead 2`
# never sends them, so planning them as released makes the run planned here the
# run replayed there. Replay it into the emulator with
#
#   uv run --with websocket-client scripts/psp-trace.py --script \
#       verification/scenarios/talons-junction-pad-0.inputs --script-lead 2
#
# **Untested against the original.** See docs/tools/autopilot-planning.md.

2 none
8 cross right r
16 cross right
5 cross
37 cross left
4 cross
30 cross right
4 cross
36 cross left
5 cross
14 cross right
60 cross
